  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound verb from {飼|か}う (to keep/raise an animal) + {慣|な}らす (to accustom). The passive form {飼|か}い{慣|な}らされた is commonly used as a modifier meaning \"tamed\" or \"domesticated.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {動物|どうぶつ}を{飼|か}い{慣|な}らす (to tame an animal)\n- {飼|か}い{慣|な}らされた{鳥|とり} (a tamed bird)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {手懐|てなず}ける: to tame — emphasizes winning over trust through gentleness\n- {家畜化|かちくか}する: to domesticate — more scientific/formal term",
